  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The tilted (3+2) verify branch in `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` starts its local stock cap at negative infinity.\n- The cap is the maximum local height of the projected stock box and model box corners.\n- The world stock top (`stock_top_z - oz`) is no longer a lower bound for the local cap.\n- A new suite `crates/app/tests/tilt_stock_cap.rs` pins the fix.\n- A decision file `docs/decisions/3004-local-stock-cap.md` records the choice.\n\n## Cause\n\n`stock_top_z` is a height along world Z.\nThe tilted branch used it, minus the plane origin's Z, as the start value of the local cap.\nThe projected corners could only raise this value.\nOn a side plane (A +90 or A -90) of a 60 x 60 x 70 blank, the real local cap is 30.\nThe cap stayed at 70.\nThe shank law then named a shank 11 mm over the side face a `ShankHit`.\nThe first-traverse law named a clearance 10 mm over the face low (`FirstTraverseLow`, `top_mm: 70`).\nThe rapid law named the drop to the face `RapidInStock`.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins in `crates/app/tests/tilt_stock_cap.rs` (each runs at A +90 and A -90, with the issue's blank and `EM-0600-4FL`):\n\n- `a_side_pocket_reads_the_local_stock_cap_not_the_world_top`: a 4 mm side pocket. No `ShankHit`. Red before the fix: `[ShankHit { at: 2, part: false }, ShankHit { at: 3, .. }, ShankHit { at: 4, .. }, ShankHit { at: 5, .. }, FirstTraverseLow { at: 0, height_mm: 40.0, top_mm: 70.0, .. }]`.\n- `a_side_slot_reads_its_clearance_against_the_local_cap`: a 4 mm side slot. No warnings. Red before the fix: `[RapidInStock { at: 1 }, FirstTraverseLow { at: 0, height_mm: 40.0, top_mm: 70.0, fixture: false }]`.\n- `a_shank_that_enters_the_side_face_still_convicts`: a 20 mm side pocket. The shank foot is 5 mm under the face. `ShankHit` stays. Green before and after.\n\nMutation check: with `generate.rs` from upstream/main, the first two pins fail and the third passes. With the fix, all three pass.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (117 steps, 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The fix changes warnings only. It does not change a toolpath.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy`) did not run.\n- An oblique plane (not a multiple of 90 degrees) keeps the conservative box cap. The issue names this as a separate limitation.\n- A material with no facets gives an inverted model box. Its projected corners give a very high cap (an over-report), as before. No test covers this case.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs touch `generate.rs`, in different lines of `run_job_arms`. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\n- #2997 and #3082: the `first_traverse::Over` line that reads `st_local`.\n- #3087: the `fidelity_law::tightened` lines.\n- #3065, #3059, #3058: other lines of the same file.\n\nChangelog: A 3+2 side operation (A +90 / A -90) reads the stock's cap along its own tool axis, so a shank or clearance clear of the side face is no longer named a collision.\n\nFixes #3004\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
